H('52.c.2.A',3,"Why collect images of ancient coins and statues in a project?","they show how people lived and what they valued",["they replace all text","they are always fake","they have no meaning"],"Artifacts are primary evidence.")
H('52.c.2.B',3,"Compiling written ideas and representations means:","gathering and organizing notes and sources",["throwing away notes","copying one page","hiding ideas"],"Compiling brings materials together.")
H('52.c.2.B',3,"An annotated list of sources helps a researcher:","keep track of what each source offers",["avoid reading","lose track of facts","add errors"],"Annotation records each source's value.")
H('52.c.2.C',4,"Drawing a conclusion from a range of sources requires:","comparing what each source says",["trusting the first source only","ignoring contradictions","skipping reading"],"Conclusions rest on evidence from many sources.")
H('52.c.2.C',4,"When two sources disagree, a careful researcher should:","examine why they differ",["pick one at random","delete both","stop researching"],"Disagreement is a chance to analyze evidence.")
